/*

	Anza Borrego by Collllin
	Created: 20 August 2024
	Updated: 
	
	Version: 1.0.0
	BSV: 
	Compatibility: Definitive Edition
    Inspired by Cross, fish booms, and my home desert

    East of San Diego California, pupfish are trapped in small ponds. As holdovers from the last ice age,
    they have adapted to arid conditions by burrowing in mud to buffer the desert's extreme temperature swings.
    The only shelter from the sun lies under the palm trees surrounding these shallow ponds.
    The rest of the Anza Borrego desert basin remains wide open. It is namd for the Spanish explorer,
    Juan Bautista de Anza, and for the numberous Penninsular Bighorn Sheep, borrego in Spanish.


    Fish ponds spawn in the corners with unwallable terrains at the entrance
    Walls are not permitted to be constructed on beach terrain
    Center paths can be walled. TC positions prevent war galleys from ranging TCs.
    Ponds are filled with pupfish (shorefish)
    Most wildlife is found in the creosote shrub (bush B)
    All creosote can be chopped and replaced with building foundations.

*/

start_random
    percent_chance 50 #define spawn_A
    percent_chance 50 #define spawn_B
end_random


<PLAYER_SETUP>

direct_placement

#const BASE_TERRAIN 14 /*Desert*/
#const ORANGE_DESERT 6 /* Dirt */
#const GRASS_SPROUT 41 /*Dirt, Savannah*/
#const PALM_GRASS 112 /*Forest, Palm Grass*/
#const CHAP 1053 /*Bush B, represents creosote*/
#const POND_GRAVEL 81 /*Beach, wet gravel*/
#const CREOSOTE 80 /*Desert, sand */
#const DESERT_PAVEMENT 46 /* Quicksand, unbuildable */
#const DESERT_GRAVEL 102 /* Desert, Gravel */
#const TC_BEACH 79 /*non-nav beach*/


/*prevent walling on beach */
effect_amount SET_ATTRIBUTE WALL_CLASS ATTR_TERRAIN_ID 4
effect_amount SET_ATTRIBUTE GATE_CLASS ATTR_TERRAIN_ID 4                            


<LAND_GENERATION>

base_terrain BASE_TERRAIN

